**D2 — profile fail-closed.** `compute_profile` now refuses non-list / empty / non-string / duplicated axes as typed `ProfileVeto` (unknown axes stay `UnsupportedSurface`) before any escalation math, and returns one normalised list that `profile_record` consumes verbatim — so the escalation basis and the emitted record can no longer disagree.

**D3 — risk honesty.** `risk_assessment="NOT_ASSESSED"` when no evidence, never `LOW_RISK_VERIFIED`. Since `ProfileBinding.schema.json` does not declare the property, adding it would be a breaking change — so it rides in the existing `_profile_meta` sidecar. `vetoes` stays `[]`: no veto evidence exists.

